n.properties</text><rect x="89" y="184" width="179" height="30" rx="8" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="179" y="203" fill="var(--text)" font-size="10.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle">Running the application</text><rect x="13" y="82" width="158" height="30" rx="8" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--text)" stroke-width="1.2"/><text x="92" y="101" fill="var(--text)" font-size="10.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle">Spring Boot DevTools</text></svg></div></div>
<div class="callout callout-why">
 <div class="callout-label">◆ WHY THIS MATTERS</div>
 <p>Spring Boot is the framework you'll spend most of this course inside. Knowing what it actually is — auto-configuration plus opinionated defaults plus an embedded server — explains why projects 'just work' once set up correctly, and why they fail mysteriously when assumptions break.</p>
</div>

<h3>Core concepts</h3>
<p><strong>1. Spring Boot vs Spring Framework.</strong> Spring Framework is the core IoC container, plus integrations for web, data, and security. Spring Boot wraps Spring Framework with auto-configuration, an embedded Tomcat, sensible defaults, and starter dependencies. You almost never use raw Spring Framework today; Spring Boot is the modern entry.</p>
<p><strong>2. Auto-configuration — the magic.</strong> Spring Boot inspects your classpath. If H2 is present, it configures an in-memory datasource. If MySQL is present plus connection properties, it configures MySQL. If Spring Web is present, it starts an embedded server. The 'magic' is: defaults you didn't have to write.</p>
<p><strong>3. Spring Initializr — start.spring.io.</strong> The web tool generates a project skeleton: pick Java version, build tool, dependencies (Web, JPA, MySQL Driver, Lombok, etc.). Download zip, open in IDE. Fastest way to start any Spring Boot project; used in this course's PA.</p>
<p><strong>4. The pom.xml in brief.</strong> Maven's project file. &lt;parent points to spring-boot-starter-parent (gives sensible plugin and dependency defaults). &lt;dependencies lists starters. &lt;build includes spring-boot-maven-plugin to package the executable JAR. You mostly add and remove dependencies; the rest is generated.</p>
<p><strong>5. application.properties.</strong> src/main/resources/application.properties. Configures port, datasource, logging, JPA, anything. server.port=8080. spring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/appdb. Spring Boot reads it at startup. application.yml is the YAML alternative — same effect, more readable for nested config.</p>
<p><strong>6. Running the application.</strong> From IntelliJ: right-click the @SpringBootApplication class → Run. From the command line: ./mvnw spring-boot:run, or build and java -jar target/app.jar. Embedded Tomcat starts; logs show the URL (http://localhost:8080).</p>
<p><strong>7. Spring Boot DevTools.</strong> Optional dependency that auto-restarts the app when classes change. Speeds development. Should not be in production builds — it slows startup and changes classloader behavior. Add it to dev only.</p>

<div class="callout callout-warning">
 <div class="callout-label">⚠ COMMON PITFALLS</div>
 <ul>
 <li>Generating a project without picking the right starter dependencies — adding them later works but is more error-prone.</li>
 <li>Editing application.properties and forgetting that changes need a restart (unless DevTools is on).</li>
 <li>Mixing Spring Boot auto-configuration with hand-written XML config — works but defeats the point.</li>
 <li>Building a fat JAR without the spring-boot-maven-plugin — the resulting JAR isn't executable as a fat JAR.</li>
 </ul>
</div>

<h3>Quick recap</h3>
<p>Spring Boot is Spring Framework + auto-configuration + embedded server + starter dependencies. Generate projects with Spring Initializr. pom.xml lists dependencies; application.properties configures behavior. Run from IDE or `mvnw spring-boot:run`. DevTools speeds development but isn't for production. The framework's value is convention over configuration — embrace it.</p>

<h3>Glossary</h3>
<dl>
 <dt><span class="key-term">Spring Boot</span></dt>
 <dd>Opinionated framework on Spring providing auto-configuration and embedded server.</dd>
 <dt><span class="key-term">Auto-configuration</span></dt>
 <dd>Spring Boot's classpath-driven setup of beans and integrations.</dd>
 <dt><span class="key-term">Spring Initializr</span></dt>
 <dd>start.spring.io — generates a Spring Boot project skeleton.</dd>
 <dt><span class="key-term">application.properties</span></dt>
 <dd>Spring Boot's main configuration file in src/main/resources.</dd>
 <dt><span class="key-term">Starter dependency</span></dt>
 <dd>Curated bundle of Spring Boot dependencies for a feature area (web, data-jpa, security).</dd>
</dl>"},"D288/ch2/s2":{"body":"<div class="vl" data-defglance="1"><div class="vl-box vl-rule def-glance"><div class="t">📖 DEFINITIONS AT A GLANCE — key terms in this section</div></div><table><tr><th style="width:32%">Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr><tr><td><b>Inversion of Control</b></td><td>classes don't create their dependencies — something else hands them in</td></tr><tr><td><b>Dependency Injection</b></td><td>the mechanism for "handing in" — constructor, setter, or field</td></tr><tr><td><b>Prefer constructor injection</b></td><td>explicit, testable, makes deps final</td></tr></table><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--text-3);margin:-6px 0 14px">Full lesson with examples below ⬇️ — nothing removed.</div></div><div class="vl" data-figure="auto" style="margin:18px 0;"><div style="font-weight:700; font-size:12.5px; letter-spacing:0.05em; margin-bottom:6px;">📊 FIGURE — the steps, in order</div><div style="border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; background:var(--surface-2); padding:14px 10px; overflow-x:auto;"><svg viewBox="0 0 640 178" style="width:100%; max-width:640px; display:block; margin:0 auto; font-family:inherit;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><defs><marker id="fa" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0,1 L9,5 L0,9 z" fill="var(--text-3)"/></marker></defs><rect x="12" y="10" width="118" height="56" rx="8" fill="var(--accent)" fill-opacity="0.12" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.4"/><text x="20" y="24" fill="var(--text-3)" font-size="10" font-weight="700">1</text><text x="71" y="40" fill="var(--text)" font-size="10.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle">Container starts</text><text x="71" y="54" fill="var(--text)" font-size="10.5" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle">up</text><line x1="130" y1="38" x2="164" y2="38" stroke="var(--text-3)" stroke-width="1.3" marker-end="url(#fa)"/><rect x="166" y="10" width="118" height="56" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--text)" stroke